---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE, SITE_DOMAIN } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How NetWageTax handles information: calculations run in your browser and are never stored, plus our disclosures on log files, cookies, and third-party advertising."
>
  <div class="border-b border-slate-200 bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-16">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500">Effective and last updated: {LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="prose-page mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains what information NetWageTax (“NetWageTax,” “we,” “us,” or “our”) collects when you
      visit {SITE_DOMAIN} (the “Site”), how that information is used, and the choices you have. By using the Site, you
      agree to the practices described in this policy.
    </p>

    <h2 id="summary">The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Your calculator entries never leave your device.</strong> All calculations run locally in your web
        browser. We do not transmit, store, or log the income, tips, overtime, filing status, or any other figures you
        enter.
      </li>
      <li><strong>We never ask for personal identifiers</strong> such as your name, Social Security number, or employer.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>We do not sell your personal information</strong>, and we do not require an account to use any tool.
      </li>
      <li>
        Like most websites, our hosting provider records standard technical log data, and third-party advertising
        partners may use cookies to serve ads. Details and opt-out options are below.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="calculations">1. Calculator data: zero retention</h2>
    <p>
      Our calculators are client-side applications. When you enter numbers into a tool, the math is performed by
      JavaScript running in your own browser. Those values are not sent to our servers or to any third party, are not
      saved in cookies or browser storage by our tools, and disappear when you close or reload the page. Because we
      never receive this data, we cannot view, retrieve, share, or delete it on your behalf.
    </p>
    <p>
      Please do not enter information into free-text fields that you would not want displayed on your own screen. We
      do not ask for, and our tools do not need, any information that identifies you personally.
    </p>

    <h2 id="logs">2. Log files</h2>
    <p>
      Like virtually every website, the Site is served by a hosting provider whose servers automatically record certain
      technical information when your browser requests a page. These server logs may include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Internet Protocol (IP) address</li>
      <li>Browser type and version, and operating system</li>
      <li>Referring and exit pages</li>
      <li>Date and time of the request</li>
      <li>The page or file requested and the response status</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This information is used to operate and secure the Site, diagnose technical problems, prevent abuse, and
      understand aggregate traffic trends. It is not linked to the figures you enter in any calculator. Log data is
      retained only as long as reasonably necessary for these purposes or as required by our hosting provider’s
      standard retention schedule.
    </p>

    <h2 id="cookies">3. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>
      Cookies are small text files placed on your device by a website. Similar technologies include web beacons,
      pixels, and local storage. NetWageTax’s own calculators do not set cookies. However, third-party services that
      help us operate and fund the Site may use cookies and similar technologies, as described below.
    </p>
    <p>
      Most browsers let you block or delete cookies through their settings. Blocking cookies will not prevent our
      calculators from working, but it may affect the relevance of the ads you see.
    </p>

    <h2 id="advertising">4. Advertising and Google AdSense</h2>
    <p>
      NetWageTax is free to use and is supported by advertising. We use, or may use, Google AdSense and other
      third-party advertising vendors to display ads on the Site. When ads are shown:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this Site and
        other websites.
      </li>
      <li>
        Google’s use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visits to
        this Site and/or other sites on the Internet.
      </li>
      <li>
        You may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting Google’s{' '}
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Ads Settings</a>. You can
        also opt out of some third-party vendors’ use of cookies for personalized advertising at{' '}
        <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">www.aboutads.info/choices</a>{' '}
        or, in the European Economic Area, at{' '}
        <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">www.youronlinechoices.eu</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        To learn how Google uses information from sites that use its services, see{' '}
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Advertising partners do not receive the values you enter into our calculators, because that information never
      leaves your browser. Where required by law, we will request your consent before non-essential advertising
      cookies are placed.
    </p>

    <h2 id="analytics">5. Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We may use privacy-respecting analytics services to understand, in aggregate, which pages are visited and how
      visitors find the Site. Any such service receives only standard technical and usage information (similar to the
      log data described above), never the values entered into our calculators. If we add an analytics provider that
      uses cookies, we will update this policy to name it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="use">6. How we use information</h2>
    <p>We use the limited information described above to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Deliver, maintain, and improve the Site and its tools</li>
      <li>Monitor performance and fix errors</li>
      <li>Detect and prevent fraud, abuse, and security incidents</li>
      <li>Display advertising that keeps the Site free</li>
      <li>Respond to messages you choose to send us</li>
      <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="sharing">7. How information is shared</h2>
    <p>We do not sell or rent personal information. We share information only:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>With service providers (such as hosting and advertising vendors) that help us operate the Site</li>
      <li>When required by law, subpoena, or other legal process</li>
      <li>To protect the rights, property, or safety of NetWageTax, our users, or the public</li>
      <li>In connection with a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets, subject to this policy</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="us-rights">8. Your privacy rights (U.S. residents)</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on your state of residence, including California, Colorado, Connecticut, Virginia, Utah, Texas, and
      other states with consumer privacy laws, you may have the right to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Know what categories of personal information we collect and how we use it</li>
      <li>Request access to, correction of, or deletion of personal information we hold about you</li>
      <li>Opt out of the “sale” or “sharing” of personal information, or its use for targeted advertising</li>
      <li>Not be discriminated against for exercising these rights</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA), the
      use of third-party advertising cookies may be considered “sharing” for cross-context behavioral advertising. You
      can opt out using the browser and industry tools listed in Section 4, or by enabling a Global Privacy Control
      (GPC) signal in your browser, which we treat as a valid opt-out request where required by law.
    </p>
    <p>
      To make a request, email us at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Because we collect very
      little information, and none that identifies you by name, we may be unable to locate data associated with you.
      We will respond within the time frame required by applicable law.
    </p>

    <h2 id="children">9. Children’s privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The Site is intended for a general audience and is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly
      collect personal information from children under 13, consistent with the Children’s Online Privacy Protection
      Act (COPPA). If you believe a child has provided us personal information, contact us and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="security">10. Security</h2>
    <p>
      The Site is served over HTTPS. Because your calculator entries are processed only on your device, they are never
      exposed to transmission or storage on our systems. No method of transmission over the Internet is completely
      secure, however, and we cannot guarantee absolute security of log or technical data handled by our providers.
    </p>

    <h2 id="links">11. Third-party links</h2>
    <p>
      The Site may link to external websites, such as IRS.gov. We are not responsible for the privacy practices of
      those sites and encourage you to review their policies.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">12. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the “last updated” date above.
      Material changes will be noted prominently on the Site. Continued use of the Site after an update constitutes
      acceptance of the revised policy.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">13. Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
